# Godot 4.7

- Engine is Godot 4.7 stable. GDScript is typed (`var n: int`, explicit returns). The project renderer is GL Compatibility.
- `scripts/core/` extends `RefCounted` only. No `Node`, scenes, `get_node`, or `Input` there.
- `scripts/view/` is rendering and input. Static layout lives in `.tscn`. Read nodes with `%UniqueName` and `@onready`. Do not build UI in code.
- The root viewport is 2560×1440. Stretch is `canvas_items` with aspect `expand`, fractional scale, and hidpi on. The window is resizable. The top bar is anchored to the full width and shows `%ManaLabel` (`Mana: N (+M/turn)`), the turn (`Turn` plus `%TurnLabel` `N / turn_limit`), and `%Score0` `%Score1` `%Score2` (one live score per player). `camera.default_zoom` is 0.72 so the map fills that window. Do not hardcode the window size in scripts.
- Repeated controls are instanced scenes. `scenes/ui/menu_button.tscn` is the menu button.
- Tunables live only in `config/game_config.json`. `GameConfig.load_file()` push_errors and quits when a key is missing or mistyped. Restart loads the file again.
- Hex math is axial `(q, r)` in `scripts/core/hex.gd`. `+q` is east, `+r` is southeast. The `TileMapLayer` uses odd-r offset: `TILE_SHAPE_HEXAGON`, `TILE_LAYOUT_STACKED`, `TILE_OFFSET_AXIS_HORIZONTAL`.
- Tile size and texture origin live only on `assets/art/bebop_tileset.tres`: face `(128, 108)`, region `(128, 116)`, `texture_origin (0, -4)`. The art is already isometric. Do not squash it and do not copy those numbers into config or scripts.
- Hover uses `TileMapLayer.local_to_map` on that TileSet. `Hex.pixel_to_hex` must keep matching it. The highlight texture is `assets/art/tile_highlight.png`.
- New Game calls `GameSetup.start`. `map.seed` 0 rolls a seed and prints `map seed: N`. Map generation, starts, players, fog, movement, founding, city turns, combat, mana, spells, score, and win/loss live in `scripts/core/` (`map_generator.gd`, `map_state.gd`, `player_state.gd`, `fog_state.gd`, `game_setup.gd`, `pathfinder.gd`, `map_city.gd`, `city_rules.gd`, `combat.gd`, `spells.gd`, `score.gd`, `match_result.gd`, `game_log.gd`). `CityRules` is yield, growth, and border math. `CityRules.city_mana` is the per-city mana rate. `PlayerState.mana` is the pool, starting at `players.starting_mana`. `Combat` is the damage formula. `SpellRules` is spell area, range, and reject reasons. `ScoreRules` is the score formula and the tie ranking. `GameSetup` applies the queue, healing, attacks, mana income, casts, elimination, and the match result. `players.starting_units` is settler then warrior. The settler takes the start tile. Each later unit takes the nearest free passable tile, because a tile holds one unit, except a captured settler sharing the capturer's tile.
- `GameSetup.spawn_unit(player, type, pos)` is the only unit constructor. `pos` is an odd-r offset cell. Pathfinding stays axial inside `Pathfinder` and converts at the `GameSetup` boundary.
- Fog is per player: unrevealed, revealed, visible. Do not paint a land atlas on an unrevealed cell. Dim only revealed-but-not-visible land. Unit vision is `fog.unit_vision`. City vision is the territory radius plus `fog.city_vision_beyond_border`. Units are instances of `scenes/actors/unit.tscn` under the y-sorted `Actors` node, placed with `map_to_local`, tinted with `assets/art/team_tint.gdshader`. Each sprite sits on the cell center. `scenes/actors/hp_bar.tscn` is the HP bar and hides when max HP is 0. Hide units on tiles the viewer cannot currently see. Draw a rival city, and the border segments of an owned tile, once that tile has been explored.
- Found is an order on `%AbilityBar` (hotkey `found_city`, B). The button tooltip is the core reason while it is disabled. Move highlights, city markers, border segments, building markers, and construction markers are instances of `scenes/view/move_highlight.tscn`, `city_marker.tscn`, `border_segment.tscn`, `building_marker.tscn`, and `construction_marker.tscn`. The highlight sprite offset is read from the TileSet. `players.city_names` is one non-empty name list per player.
- `%CityPanel` opens when the human left-clicks their city and stays open while a unit is selected. A cast refreshes it, the selected unit's move highlights, and the combat preview in the same frame. It shows food, production, mana from that city, the growth bar, the border clock, and the production queue. That mana line is `CityRules.city_mana`, the same number `GameSetup.mana_per_turn` sums into the top bar. Build buttons are `menu_button` instances. Queue rows are `scenes/ui/queue_row.tscn`. A building is queued by clicking its button, then a highlighted border tile that is not the center. That tile shows `construction_marker.tscn` until the building finishes, the item is cancelled, the tile is flooded, or the city is captured. Only the human's queued buildings are drawn. Details are in `docs/cities.md`.
- Left click selects the human unit on that tile. A city on that tile comes after the unit. Right click moves onto a highlighted tile, including a capture of a 0 HP city or a lone settler, and does not attack. `%AbilityBar` shows while one of the human's units is selected. Its buttons are instances of `scenes/ui/ability_button.tscn`: abilities in config order, then Skip, Fortify, and Found. A grey button's tooltip is the core reason. Clicking a ready ability targets it. The preview reuses the spell highlight path. Sprint (`effect` `move`, `target` `self`) paints the post-bonus reachable tiles in the move tint and does not change AP until confirm, which is the unit's tile or the button again. Afterward the unit is movement-only: abilities and orders grey with `Can only move`, the AP label may exceed the pool, and right-click still moves. End Turn clears that flag and refills from the unit's AP. A unit at 0 AP is done for the turn (`GameSetup.unit_turn_done`): the sprite dims (`self_modulate` alpha 0.55, HP bar still opaque) until that refill, the selection line reads `Done` when the order is none, and the selection jumps to the next human unit that still needs orders, centering the camera without changing zoom. `%NextUnitButton` (Period, `next_unit`) cycles that list. Enter and End Turn show `N units need orders (Enter)` while any remain. The first press jumps to the next unit and arms the confirm; a second press on that same unit with no state change is `End anyway (Enter)` and ends the turn. One press ends it when none remain. Skip and Fortify look done too and still do not set `acted`. Shield Bash also paints its push hex from `ability_preview` (place tint when open, invalid tint when blocked). Volley is a `radius` ability: the aimed tile must be in range and currently visible, and the disk hits visible enemy units and visible enemy cities. Friendly cities in that disk are not hit, and a city does not move. `%CombatPreview` shows damage and counter-damage only while an ability is targeted, one `Damage N` per hit when several targets are struck, plus `Push` or `No push` when the ability pushes. Melee counter-damage follows `deals_counter`. Strike still counters. Shield Bash does not, and it pushes a living unit one hex directly away unless that hex is off the map, impassable, occupied, or a city. Left click on a legal tile calls `use_ability`. Right click or Esc cancels targeting. Enter (`end_turn`) ends the turn through the same path as `%EndTurnButton`. The first press warns when a human unit still has AP and no order; the second confirms. Skip (`skip_unit`, S) needs no AP and sets AP to 0 without setting `acted`. Fortify (`fortify_unit`, F) and Found need at least 1 AP, then set AP to 0. Fortify does not set `acted`. The bar tooltip shows `Needs at least 1 AP` when that order is refused. End Turn resolves every city's growth, production, and border claim, then adds each player's snapshotted city mana to that player's pool, heals cities that were not attacked and idle units, applies flat volcanic damage, ticks spell cooldowns and ability cooldowns, then either ends the game (human eliminated, conquest, or the turn-limit ranking) or increments the turn and refills movement. A player with no cities and no settlers is eliminated and their units are removed. Founding does not eliminate. The top bar never shows a turn past `turn_limit`. Victory and Defeat read `MatchResult.latest`. There is no debug key that opens those scenes. Details are in `docs/win_loss.md`. A unit on volcanic ground shows `Volcanic: -N HP at end of turn` on `%VolcanicWarning`; only that line is amber. Creating water removes a finished building on that tile when `buildings.water_destroys_building` is true, always drops a queued building aimed at the tile, and refreshes the city panel and top bar through the cast refresh. A Mana Well finished this turn is paid on the next End Turn. Enter does nothing while the in-game menu is open. Details are in `docs/combat.md` and `docs/cities.md`.
- Win and loss: `GameSetup.score` uses `score.per_tile`, `score.per_city`, and `score.per_population` on border tiles (including the center and water), cities, and population. `%Score0` `%Score1` `%Score2` show it. Conquest and human elimination end the game immediately. End Turn on turn `turn_limit` ranks by score, then `ties.order`, and the human must be strictly first. See `docs/win_loss.md`.
- `%SpellBar` / `%SpellButtons` sit under the top bar. Buttons are instances of `scenes/ui/spell_button.tscn`, one per config spell. A button's mana check reads `PlayerState.mana` through `GameSetup.spell_block_reason`. Click a ready spell to target. Highlights reuse `scenes/view/move_highlight.tscn` and show the exact radius or line in the new land's color. A tile where water would destroy a building also gets a smaller gold highlight, and the tooltip counts those buildings. Left-click casts. Right-click or Esc cancels targeting. Choosing a spell cancels ability targeting, and choosing an ability cancels the spell. Esc toggles the menu only when neither is armed. `spells.spells_require_revealed_target` rejects an unrevealed tile. Explored and visible both count as revealed. Details are in `docs/spells.md`.
- Commit `.import` and `.uid` files. Do not commit `.godot/`.
- A fresh checkout has no class cache. Run `godot --headless --path . --import` before tests or the game.
- A game log is one JSON Lines file per New Game or Restart: `user://logs/game_<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>_<seed>.jsonl` when `log.enabled` is true. `log.directory` is the folder. `GameLog` builds the `start`, `cast`, and `end` dictionaries. `GameLog.Writer` appends them. `GameSetup.open_log` writes `start` and prints `game log: <absolute path>`. A successful `cast_spell` appends one `cast`. `_finish` appends one `end` from `MatchResult` and stores the absolute path on `MatchResult.log_path`. `%LogPath` on Victory and Defeat shows that path. A write failure is a warning and play continues. An abandoned game has no `end` line. Details are in `docs/game_log.md`.
- Tests, from the repo root: `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/run_tests.gd`, then the missing-key script (it must exit non-zero), then `--quit-after 120` on `res://scenes/main_menu.tscn` and `res://scenes/game.tscn`, then `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/smoke_game.gd`, then `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/smoke_log.gd`, then `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/soak_games.gd` (`SOAK OK`). Unit tests disable logging or point `log.directory` at a temp dir. `GameLog.directory_override` and `GameConfig.path_override` are the test seams. They must not write `user://logs`. The soak's seeds, invariants, and the ticket 30 sidestep are in `docs/stability.md`.
- If you change architecture, conventions, or these commands, update `AGENTS.md`, this file, and `docs/`.
